papers.problem:
The diffuse flux of ultrahigh-energy neutrinos ($E_{
u}\gtrsim 100\,\mathrm{PeV}$ in the abstract; $E_{
u}\gtrsim 10^{17}\,\mathrm{eV}$ in the introduction), produced by photohadronic and hadronic interactions of extragalactic UHECRs ($E_{\mathrm{CR}}\gtrsim 10^{18}\,\mathrm{eV}$), is uncertain by orders of magnitude. A KM3NeT candidate at $220^{+570}_{-110}\,\mathrm{PeV}$ contrasts with existing limits near $E_{
u}^{2}\Phi_{
u}\lesssim 10^{-8}\,\mathrm{GeV}\,\mathrm{cm}^{-2}\,\mathrm{s}^{-1}\,\mathrm{sr}^{-1}$ at $1\,\mathrm{EeV}$, which require $\gtrsim 10^{2}\,\mathrm{km}^{3}$ effective volume.

papers.method:
A 50-event Ia-CSM sample (narrow Balmer lines with ${m FWHM}\lesssim2000\,\mathrm{km\,s^{-1}}$ on a diluted Ia continuum; discoveries 2016–2025) uses ATLAS, ZTF, and Gaia photometry. Fluxes are uncertainty-weighted and stacked every 0.5 day; detections use $\sigma=F_
u/F_{
u,m err}$, with $\ge3\sigma$ magnitudes and otherwise $3\sigma$ limits (AB zero-point 23.9 mag). A 2D Gaussian process measures peaks and rise/decline times at 10% flux intervals for $F_
u/F_{
u,m err}\ge3$. Blackbody SEDs give thermal and 3250–8900 Å optical luminosities under $H_0=71\,\mathrm{km\,s^{-1}\,Mpc^{-1}}$, $\Omega_\Lambda=0.7$, $\Omega_m=0.3$, with mostly Galactic extinction only ($R_V=3.1$). Morphology is compared with IIn templates and 2D CSM-interaction simulations.
